{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781585629,"nonce":"Q3piLWXOyvoexYZdJTilxemmOX4=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFmx4CQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/282","origin":"github"},"title":"bizzyboat URDF: add measured waterline frame + correct sidescan mount offsets (2026-06-15)","message":"## Summary\nUpdate the bizzyboat URDF (`bizzyboat_project11/urdf/`) with offsets **measured during the 2026-06-15 Lake Massabesic survey**, replacing approximate/assumed values:\n\n1. **Add a `bizzy/waterline` frame** (new) — the measured water surface relative to `base_link`.\n2. **Correct the Garmin sidescan mount offsets** — currently approximate.\n\n## 1. Waterline frame (measured — ready)\nDerived from the draft-team measurements (2026-06-15):\n- draft reference point: **+0.180 m** above `base_link`\n- waterline: **0.150 m below** that ref point (water 15 cm down)\n- ⇒ **waterline = +0.030 m above `base_link`** (base_link sits ~30 mm below the surface)\n\nAdd a fixed frame off `base_link`:\n```xml\n\u003c!-- Measured water surface, 2026-06-15 Massabesic: ref point +0.180 m above\n     base_link, water 0.150 m below ref =\u003e waterline +0.030 m above base_link. --\u003e\n\u003clink name=\"bizzy/waterline\"/\u003e\n\u003cjoint name=\"base_to_waterline\" type=\"fixed\"\u003e\n  \u003cparent link=\"bizzy/base_link\"/\u003e\n  \u003cchild link=\"bizzy/waterline\"/\u003e\n  \u003corigin xyz=\"0 0 0.030\" rpy=\"0 0 0\"/\u003e\n\u003c/joint\u003e\n```\nSupports the datum / sea-surface reference work (relates to #278) and sounding reduction (waterline ↔ base_link tie).\n\n## 2. Sidescan mount offsets (measured values PENDING)\nCurrent placement in `bizzyboat.urdf.xacro` is **approximate**:\n```xml\n\u003cxacro:garmin_sidescan parent=\"bizzy/base_link\" name=\"garmin_sidescan\"\n  x=\"0.15\" y=\"0.0\" z=\"-0.30\"/\u003e   \u003c!-- \"~0.15 m forward, flush hull underside; z=-0.30 hull bottom\" --\u003e\n```\nReplace `x/y/z` with the **measured** offsets. **The measured values were not found in the 2026-06-15 dev/field/operator logs — to be provided** (operator to supply, or point to where they were recorded). Orientation stays in TF (the `sidescan.xacro` macro handles channel rpy), per the sensor-driver convention — offsets only here.\n\n## Notes\n- github-origin → worktree + PR.\n- Regenerate `bizzyboat_project11/docs/bizzyboat_offsets.svg` (via `bizzyboat_offsets_gen.py`) after the change so the offsets diagram stays in sync.\n- Part of the 2026-06-15 deployment (#277) follow-ups.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}